"source": "Google Earth web historical imagery: aerials of 30 Jul 2023 (anchor), 30 Mar 2022 and 30 Apr 2019, straight-down captures at 0.132 m a pixel. Each date's painted line traced along 1440 rays; the other two dates lined up on the 2023 line by the line itself (2022: shift -0.04,-1.18 m, rms 0.34; 2019: -1.40,-1.09 m, rms 0.96) and the median taken. Goals: 50 m arc then the 6.4 x 9 m goal square; 2023 and 2019 agree to 0.09 m after lining up.",
